  "preconditions": [
    "Explicit parsed artifact candidates, actual source bytes, exact selected mapping, complete supplied TargetModel and explicit native creation envelopes/actor/time. Trusted target policy/gates are caller registrations, not source data."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Plan new and matched artifacts through real mapping selection, native lookup, conflict evaluation and the ordinary complete-target Change Plan service.",
    "Inspect exact byte/canonical bindings, operations, native IDs, regular metadata/history, preserved local fields, attachment references, skipped objects, unresolved conflicts and individual losses.",
    "Verify normal saved-plan target equivalence, blocking target gates, passive detached reports and isolated Core/PYZ availability without filesystem writes.",
    "Reassess saved canonical import envelopes against independently supplied current source bytes, format, parsed candidates, mapping, basis and explicit request metadata/policy; rerun all current target gates.",
    "Reject stale raw/semantic inputs and forged operations, results, losses, success or authority claims; preserve invalid reports, original input ownership and project/operational inventory. Verify Core/PYZ availability."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "`specroad import plan <FORMAT> <INPUT>` MUSS Eingabeformat, Mapping, neue und aktualisierte Artefakte, Konflikte, Informationsverluste, Anhänge, Diagnosen, einen ausführbaren Change Plan und die erwartete Zielmodellwurzel ausgeben, ohne den Projektstand zu verändern.",
    "scope": "14.d.W implements an owned artifact-import-plan-v1 observation from explicit parsed artifact candidates. Actual mapping bytes, native-owner lookup and the five-case policy derive regular create/update operations with explicit IDs, actor and time. The ordinary Change Plan service recomputes regular revisions/history and validates the complete supplied target. Exact input bytes, canonical and byte mapping hashes, candidate content, base/root, resource/source bindings and Change Plan hash are retained. Reports include planned created/updated IDs, skipped objects, unresolved conflicts, individual unaccepted unmapped-field losses and byte-verified existing attachment references. No-op/local/skip/reject preserve native history; safe adoption keeps the same ID and preserves unrelated fields and identities. A missing gate, divergent conflict, unaccepted loss or invalid complete target never exposes a valid executable plan. The regular saved plan reproduces the target on the same supplied model. No input parsing, filesystem completeness, authorization, transaction or completed import is claimed. 14.d.R adds assess_import_plan: strict JSON bytes are passive saved data. Full re-preparation from explicit current inputs must reproduce every bound field and observation; no expected input, actor/time, policy or gate is taken from the saved report. All source/resource bytes, candidates, untouched base members, reservations, metadata and current target checks remain bound. A changed gate result or input requires a new preparation; matching invalid reports remain non-executable. JSON envelope layout may differ, not the bound source bytes. No live inventory, source parsing, authority, transaction or import completion is claimed."
  },
